  "term": "motion parallax",
  "definition": "In cognition, motion parallax is the depth-related change in an object’s apparent motion during observer movement. In the cited context, lateral head movement makes a target appear to move in opposite directions depending on whether it is nearer than the fixation point or farther away.",
